#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167781} :activity/id #uuid "b36ed83a-cc37-5ff2-a68e-2a0e28c0b24e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048270 :topic/id #uuid "8e43115f-4416-5ec0-b698-3e53a959567b" :topic/math-academy-id 3286} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167713 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166847 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166697 :question/id #uuid "699d9c0c-bb98-5710-8d98-10b6f35ab202" :question/math-academy-id "e-8911"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9d77603-c824-5160-80fc-3d10353fe243" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048412} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049605}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167115} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167116}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability Using Bayes' Theorem"} :step/id #uuid "7e6025e7-7c05-542d-a78a-f9d7e627be29" :step/math-academy-id 33287 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167772}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167714 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166848 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166698 :question/id #uuid "284f5029-19eb-53d4-a3b7-0f66d33b9cc9" :question/math-academy-id "e-8912"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a4fee2d-88c3-5381-bd55-98990abc7df3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167117} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167119} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275200}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Conditional Probability"} :step/id #uuid "fd5da403-f379-5dee-9a50-ecafcf083c36" :step/math-academy-id 33288} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167772 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166877 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166482 :question/id #uuid "bc694d40-d150-55e6-981f-0ca6b5d91e21" :question/math-academy-id "e-10418"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c467adb-9d0e-5b33-b81e-4959e2703535" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167052} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167118}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying Bayes’ Theorem to a Situation in Context"} :step/id #uuid "7a97606a-98ac-50e6-9e3c-78ae18820b2e" :step/math-academy-id 39256 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167714}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167781 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168143 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we will generalize Bayes' theorem to deal with situations where the sample space $\\mathcal S$ is partitioned into a disjoint union of multiple events.\n\nSuppose we have three events $A_1,A_2$, and $A_3$ that form a disjoint union of the sample space $\\mathcal S$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/89/89a78ef526fcd29a59bacd4d6ae1a456a596d6616af7453f1ba530a610d9a2ac.png)\n\nNow consider an event $B$ that also lies in the sample space:\n\n![](images/da/daa96423e45f9f80897e2c2d61177eab2faff77f440921866d1b81b7ef2cfe09.png)\n\nBayes' theorem states that\n\n$$\nP(A_1 \\mid B)=\\dfrac{P(B \\mid A_1)P(A_1)}{P(B)}\n$$\n\nNow, the law of total probability tells us that\n\n$$\nP(B)=P(B \\mid A_1)P(A_1) + P(B \\mid A_2)P(A_2) + P(B \\mid A_3)P(A_3)\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Bayes' theorem, we get\n\n$$\nP(A_1 \\mid B) = \\dfrac{P(B \\mid A_1) P(A_1)}{P(B \\mid A_1)P(A_1) + P(B \\mid A_2)P(A_2) + P(B \\mid A_3)P(A_3)}\n$$\n\nUsing similar arguments, we can say that for $A_k$ for $k=1,2,3$, we have\n\n$$\nP(A_k \\mid B) = \\dfrac{P(B \\mid A_k) P(A_k)}{P(B \\mid A_1)P(A_1) + P(B \\mid A_2)P(A_2) + P(B \\mid A_3)P(A_3)}\n$$\n\nwhich is usually written more compactly as\n\n$$\nP(A_k \\mid B) = \\dfrac{P(B \\mid A_k) P(A_k)}{\\sum_{i=1}^3 P(B \\mid A_i)P(A_i)}\n$$\n\nIt's easy to see how this generalizes. If the disjoint union $A_1 \\sqcup A_2 \\sqcup \\ldots \\sqcup A_n$ covers the entire sample space, Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability gives us the following:\n\n$$\nP(A_k \\mid B) = \\dfrac{P(B \\mid A_k) P(A_k)}{\\sum_{i=1}^n P(B \\mid A_i)P(A_i)}\n$$\n\nLet's see an example of how to apply this theorem." :tutorial/id #uuid "bf17685f-9890-54cc-b8a2-15815558e87a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6969 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b6bd91e8-6598-5c56-9fa4-bf1144fc830d" :step/math-academy-id 42168 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167713}}] :activity/title "Extending Bayes' Theorem" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167047}]}
